I eat the last piece of my cinnamon roll.
It tastes really good.
But it is also very sweet.
My coffee cup is completely empty.
I am suddenly very thirsty.
I would like to have some cold water.
A young man walks past my table.
He works here in the café.
He collects empty cups and plates.
I catch his eye.
He stops at my table and smiles.
"Excuse me," I say politely.
"Yes?" answers the young man.
"May I ask for a glass of tap water?" I ask.
"Yes, of course," he says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
He takes my empty plate and cup.
He walks back to the counter.
A little later he comes with a cold glass of water.
